    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d567">

                <pb facs="0949" n="879" xml:id="pg879"/>

                <head>No. 568.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Wallace to Mr. Frelinghuysen</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1883-08-22"><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 22, 1883</date>.
                        (Received September 10.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 267.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose herewith the
                    further correspondence touching the affair of Dr. Pflaum, consisting of a note
                    from the Sublime Porte and a note from this legation, both in copy.</p>
                <p>Until a reply is had to the latter it will, of course, be impossible for the
                    President to decide upon final action proper in the case.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * * *</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>LEW. WALLACE.</signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d567-a1.xml" xpointer="d567-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d567-a2.xml" xpointer="d567-a2"/>
